Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: add minimal SC2 HK1 RBOX X4 removable-boot platform

Target Linux 6.18.57. Structural source: hkallweit linux-amlogic-sc2
3730dc06ac5eb6282995ca8f82636b106429a796, board commit79f5fc0fa7.
Board wiring source: Stock_ROM/unpacked_img/stock_dtb_1.dts, original
sc2_ah212_4g. Cross-check power-domain IDs/SMC ABI with CE linux-amlogic
a3aaaa5b0e646dcd8cf4a23d6b8d66a5292840eb and Khadas linux
ef8cd851f48356675c3e987fead999fe28f6f69d.

Expose the original 0xf0000000 usable-memory boundary of the 4GB variant.
Preserve the low firmware/BL31 ranges from the SC2 port and stock fixed
secure, DSP and framebuffer ranges as no-map. Stock ramoops lies inside
the secmon range, so it is not mapped independently. Do not transplant
Android multimedia CMA heaps or fabricate regulators.

Use existing G12A UART operations (XTAL/2 and ttyAML0); S4 UART operations
would change the device name to ttyS0. Set the SD input mux to XTAL in DT
for identification clocks rather than altering all Meson MMC hosts. SD is
limited to 50MHz/3.3V; original eMMC is disabled. Ethernet uses the stock
external RGMII PHY/reset, not the donor board internal PHY. Keep the stock
USB high-speed limit. CPU DVFS, Wi-Fi, display and media are not described.
This patch series is source enablement, not evidence of a physical boot.

---

